  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englisl Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 3,\n  \"section_title\": \"Grammar and Vocabulary (B2)\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 21,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct translation for 'It was said that she had finished her work'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) She had finished her work, it was said.\",\n        \"B) It was said that she has finished her work.\",\n        \"C) He had finished her work, it was stated.\",\n        \"D) She had finished her work; this is what was said.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 22,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses the passive voice correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) The book was read by John.\",\n        \"B) John is being read by the book.\",\n        \"C) The cake has been baked in the oven.\",\n        \"D) They are cooking for me.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 23,\n      \"question\": \"Choose the appropriate conditional form for 'If I had studied harder, I would have passed the exam.'\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Had I studied hard.\",\n        \"B) Studied more diligently.\",\n        \"C) Would have passed the exam if I had studied harder.\",\n        \"D) Had I studied hard, would I have passed.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 24,\n      \"question\": \"Which discourse marker best connects the two sentences?\"\n        \"Sentence 1: 'I think it's important to exercise regularly.'\"\n        \"Sentence 2: 'Therefore, I plan to join a gym next week.'\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) However.\",\n        \"B) Nevertheless.\",\n        \"C) Therefore.\",\n        \"D) Moreover.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 25,\n      \"question\": \"Which collocation is incorrect?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) A pair of shoes.\",\n        \"B) A dozen apples.\",\n        \"C) Three quarters of an hour.\",\n        \"D) Two halves of a ball.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"D\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 26,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent prepositional phrase is incorrect?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Because of the rain.\",\n        \"B) In spite of my protests.\",\n        \"C) Despite his excellent grades.\",\n        \"D) As a result, I decided to stay home.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"D\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 27,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a more precise lexical choice for 'It's important to maintain good hygiene.'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Keep clean.\",\n        \"B) Ensure sanitation.\",\n        \"C) Make sure to wash hands frequently.\",\n        \"D) Be mindful of germs.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 28,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following reported speech is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) He said 'I think it's important to exercise regularly.'\",\n        \"B) She stated that he had finished his work.\",\n        \"C) They were informed about the meeting time.\",\n        \"D) It was said to be a great idea.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 29,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses a dependent prepositional phrase correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I live near the park.\",\n        \"B) She writes about her experiences in a book.\",\n        \"C) He is driving to work every day.\",\n        \"D) We will meet at the corner of the street.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 30,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct use of 'therefore'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I think it's important to exercise regularly, therefore I plan to join a gym next week.\",\n        \"B) Because of the rain, in spite of my protests, I decided not to go out.\",\n        \"C) Three quarters of an hour later, they finally arrived at the station.\",\n        \"D) As a result, I was expelled from school for disciplinary reasons.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
